<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">8 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 8 September, from 1504 to 1974.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/florence" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/florence.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1504 CE <span class="tih-ago">522 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Michelangelo's David is unveiled in Florence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Michelangelo's colossal marble David was unveiled outside the Palazzo Vecchio. Carved from a block other sculptors had abandoned, it became a symbol of the Florentine Republic.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1565 CE <span class="tih-ago">461 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Ottomans abandon the Great Siege of Malta</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After nearly four months, the Ottoman army withdrew from Malta, defeated by the Knights of St John under Jean de Valette. The new capital, Valletta, was named after him.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1664 CE <span class="tih-ago">362 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Dutch hand New Amsterdam to the English</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Facing English warships and an unwilling population, Peter Stuyvesant surrendered New Amsterdam without a fight. It was renamed New York after the Duke of York.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-amsterdam">New Amsterdam</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1943 CE <span class="tih-ago">83 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Italy's armistice with the Allies is announced</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">General Eisenhower broadcast news of Italy's surrender. German troops quickly disarmed the Italian army and occupied much of the country, which became a battleground for 20 months.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1974 CE <span class="tih-ago">52 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gerald Ford pardons Richard Nixon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President Ford granted Nixon a full pardon for any crimes he 'committed or may have committed' in office. Ford said it would end the national ordeal; it damaged his own popularity.</p></div></li></ol>
